      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1771525253790,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Tic-Tac-Toe game should be played on a 3x3 grid.\nTwo players take turns marking their symbols (X or O) on the grid.\nThe first player to get three of their symbols in a row (horizontally, vertically, or diagonally) wins the game.\nIf all the cells on the grid are filled and no player has won, the game ends in a draw.\nThe game should have a user interface to display the grid and allow players to make their moves.\nThe game should handle player turns and validate moves to ensure they are legal.\nThe game should detect and announce the winner or a draw at the end of the game.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Tic-Tac-Toe game should be played on a 3x3 grid.\nTwo players take turns marking their symbols (X or O) on the grid.\nThe first player to get three of their symbols in a row (horizontally, vertically, or diagonally) wins the game.\nIf all the cells on the grid are filled and no player has won, the game ends in a draw.\nThe game should have a user interface to display the grid and allow players to make their moves.\nThe game should handle player turns and validate moves to ensure they are legal.\nThe game should detect and announce the winner or a draw at the end of the game.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
